  bootwright / cluster update-admin-creds
      Generate a fresh password for each administrator login of one cluster and update it in
      the running environment: the console administrator of OpenShift or OKD; the dashboard
      administrator, the Prometheus and Alertmanager logins behind the management gateway, and
      the Grafana admin password of a managed Ceph cluster. --login takes a comma-separated
      list of console, dashboard, prometheus, alertmanager and grafana (default: every login
      the cluster has); a listed login the cluster does not have refuses before anything
      changes. Requires a completed apply and the original administrator access. Runs the
      logins in that order, each retaining its candidate before updating the cluster; a failure
      stops the run, and its remedy names the logins left to update. Repeat an interrupted
      command to finish the same update. A Grafana update writes the new password as a new
      version of its bound Secret and holds that version in the apply's binding. Refuses
      removed accounts and external Ceph. Retrieve the updated credentials with cluster info
      --secrets --name <cluster>. --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster update-admin-creds [flags]

  Command flags
      --login  Select comma-separated administrator logins to update (default: all the cluster
               has) (values: console, dashboard, prometheus, alertmanager, grafana)
      --name   Select the exact object name (required)
      --yes    Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright cluster update-admin-creds --context lab --name cluster --login
    prometheus,alertmanager
